    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d309">

                <pb facs="0287" n="275" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg275"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845.24/515</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Adviser on International Economic
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Feis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-07-19">July 19, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Lend-Leasing of Silver to India.</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: We have discussed this
                    matter with the Senior Treasury Representative and an official of the Indian
                    Government here on Treasury business. I believe this short Memorandum of
                        Conversation<anchor n="38" xml:id="d309-f1"/> covers the main points of the
                    present situation. It was agreed that the discussion should continue directly
                    with the Treasury and the State Department should not enter into the discussion
                    until or unless it becomes deadlocked, in which case the Embassy would inform
                    us.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Feis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
